# Membrane Fetch -- configuration
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is git-ignored and should stay that way.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Claude --
# The reasoning model the brief specifies. This is the only provider the
# project uses; earlier revisions carried several stand-ins while no Anthropic
# key was available, and they have been removed.
#
# Get a key:  https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#
# It must be an API key, which begins "sk-ant-api03-". A token beginning
# "sk-ant-usr-" is a Claude Code sign-in token, not an API key: the Messages
# API rejects it with "invalid x-api-key" under every authentication scheme,
# and the Claude Code CLI reports "Not logged in". If that is what you were
# given, ask for an API key instead.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Point the agent at an engine on another host or port.
# MEMBRANE_ENGINE=http://127.0.0.1:8080
